{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/955108-inferno-demon-question","id":955108,"title":"Inferno demon question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-21T12:56:06-07:00","id":955108,"title":"Inferno demon question","content":"So this come up in a game recently... (2e rules but using Inferno)<br /> <br /> A Rank 1 Imp from Inferno, an astral Deceptor type was dwelling in a Desecrated locale and could Fetter into people it found there and Urge them. Being a sorta corrupt Goetic, it seemed to be at home usually in the Astral Space.<br /> <br /> The Imp through generating an Open condition Fettered itself on a person and the person left the Desecrated place, leaving the Imp outside of it's Influences once the Open condition timed out (assuming the Fetter can last as long as the Imp rolled it's time in successes with Strengthen Influence to make the person Open).<br /> <br /> Because the Imp is an astral creature, does it use Resonant like a spirit? And what happens if it was to go into Hibernation from essence bleed as an Inferno demon? Is it banished to Hell from whence it came, or as an astral being does it slip into the Astral Space (Oneiros or Temeros)?<br /> <br /> Just some weirdness I'd like to know more on, thanks for any and all help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:00:24-07:00","id":955211,"title":"","content":"These are my two cents; not sure if it is how it would be handled RAW:<br /> <br /> 1)I'd use Resonant as a Spirit, yes. Just for simplification's sake.<br /> <br /> 2) If it goes into Hibernation, <u>if it is important for the story</u> i usually make a scene out of that point, one moment in which something happens that would allow it to keep in the Astral or even in Twilight. If the entity is powerful, i design some situation in which the favorable outcome from the entity is hard to reach, but it has some way of achieving it. As long as it is trying to achieve its goals (and the logical situation time-span has not ended) i don't end it. If the entity achieves its goals, its back, and stronger. If not, that's it, and it is sent to Hell.<br /> <br /> It is a demon, after all, it comes from Hell, not from the Oneiros or the Temenos. It can reach those others states, yes. But its origin -and end- is Hell. At least, that's my point of view. Hope it helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}